{:steps
 [{:name "select-and-create",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :skills ["incidental-complexity-finder" "gordian" "code-shaper"],
   :thinking-level :high,
   :contributions
   [{:type :template,
     :text "You are executing the incidental-complexity simplification workflow in this repository. This workflow runs entirely in the invoking session's current inherited worktree. It selects the single highest incidental-complexity unit, captures baselines, creates a constrained behaviour-preserving refactor task in the current worktree, and emits a structured handoff. Later workflow steps review the design, create/review the plan, establish a pre-simplification characterization-test net, run a baseline/diff gate, and only then delegate simplification implementation and review in the same inherited worktree.\n\nRequired procedure:\n\n1. Confirm the current worktree context.\n   - Run `git status --short --branch` and treat the current branch/worktree as the intended refactor location.\n   - Do NOT call `work-on` and do NOT create or switch to another worktree. The caller is responsible for invoking this workflow from the intended isolated branch/worktree.\n   - If the current checkout has an ambiguous or unsafe state for an autonomous refactor, stop and report that clearly instead of switching worktrees.\n\n2. Select the target with the `incidental-complexity-finder` skill.\n   - Apply the `incidental-complexity-finder` skill to choose the single highest incidental-complexity executable unit (the `gap = lcc-total / max(cc, 1)` method, the `lcc-total >= 5.0 and gap >= 2.0` qualification filter, and the top-5 essential-vs-incidental judgment guard).\n   - Capture the chosen target's evidence (ns, var, arity, file, line range, lcc-total with per-dimension burdens, cc, gap, the local findings, and the coverage hint).\n\n3. Early stop when no unit qualifies.\n   - If no unit qualifies (nothing meets `lcc-total >= 5.0 and gap >= 2.0`, or none of the top 5 pass the judgment guard), STOP.\n   - Do NOT create a task.\n   - Do NOT create or switch worktrees.\n   - Final response must clearly say that no unit qualified, listing the candidates considered.\n   - Do not emit a `munera_task_path:` line in the no-target response.\n   - End the final response with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK` so the workflow deterministically skips every downstream design/plan/test-net/implementation step and completes directly.\n\n4. Allocate the task id and create the task directory in the current worktree.\n   - Allocate the next canonical Munera task id by scanning the CURRENT WORKTREE's `munera/open/` and `munera/closed/`: `NNN = max(NNN over open/ union closed/) + 1`, zero-padded to >= 3 digits.\n   - Create `munera/open/NNN-slug/design.md` for the generated refactor task (slug derived from the target), using the contract in step 6.\n\n5. Capture two `before` baselines into the task directory (run from the current worktree root):\n   - `before-local.json` — `bb gordian local --json` (bare, NO `--sort`) — the per-unit comprehension-burden baseline. Write it to `munera/open/NNN-slug/before-local.json`.\n   - `before-diagnose.edn` — `bb gordian diagnose --edn` — the architectural gate baseline for `gordian gate --baseline`. Write it to `munera/open/NNN-slug/before-diagnose.edn`.\n   - Note: `before-local.json` uses a DIFFERENT invocation from the selector's `local --sort total --json` ranking call; because the Phase-1 before/after comparison is keyed by `(ns, var, arity, line)`, sort order is irrelevant to baseline validity.\n   - Path resolution: Phase 1 runs `gordian gate`/`gordian local` from the worktree root (cwd), where a bare filename does not resolve. The generated `design.md` must therefore reference each baseline by its worktree-root-relative task-dir path — `munera/open/NNN-slug/before-diagnose.edn` and `munera/open/NNN-slug/before-local.json`. Record the concrete task path in the generated `design.md` so Phase-1 commands use the resolvable path rather than a bare filename.\n\n6. Generated `design.md` — the two-phase behaviour-preserving contract.\n   The generated task is a behaviour-preserving refactor (the `refactor_minimal_semantics_spec_tests` formalism), executed in two ordered phases. Its `design.md` must state:\n   - The target unit and the captured incidental-complexity evidence.\n   - Blast radius: the target unit PLUS the minimal surrounding helpers required to decomplect it; no unrelated cleanup. The net-burden acceptance below keeps this honest.\n   - Constraint: behaviour is identical — meta/spec are unchanged; existing test expectations are not weakened.\n\n   Phase 0 — establish a test safety net (gate before any refactor).\n   A behaviour-preserving refactor is unverifiable without tests that would catch a behaviour change, so refactoring is gated on sufficient coverage:\n   - Assess existing coverage of the target's observable behaviour (tests that exercise the unit directly or transitively), judged against `{nominal, edge, boundary}` per the project Test formalism.\n   - If insufficient, add characterization tests capturing CURRENT observable behaviour (state/outputs, never interactions; per `testing-without-mocks`). Adding tests that document existing behaviour does not change behaviour or spec — it strengthens the proof.\n   - These tests must be GREEN against the unmodified code before any refactoring begins.\n   - If the unit cannot be characterized safely (e.g. an untestable side-effect tangle), the task records that finding and either (a) first introduces a minimal seam to make it testable, or (b) is closed with the finding (scope drift -> close per Munera). No refactor proceeds without a green net.\n\n   Phase 1 — refactor under the green net. Decomplect the target with minimal, local, root-cause changes (not superficial extraction).\n   Objective acceptance criteria:\n   - Burden reduction (A5 — named comparison source). Re-run `bb gordian local --json` from the worktree root and compare against the stored `munera/open/NNN-slug/before-local.json` captured in this step — that file is the single authoritative baseline for every \"decreased\" check (not the selector's emitted evidence, not a fresh pre-refactor recompute). The target unit's `lcc-total` (keyed by `(ns, var, arity, line)` — the same unique key the selector's join uses; `line` disambiguates same-named null-arity `defmethod` units that share `(ns, var, arity)`, e.g. the 51 `execute-effect!` defmethods) decreased versus its `before-local.json` value.\n   - Net burden (A2 — \"touched units\" defined). \"Touched units\" means every unit whose recomputed `lcc-total` changed between `before-local.json` and the after-`local` run — i.e. the set is computed from the metric, not from the diff/touched files. This deliberately includes callers whose `dependency`/`working-set` burden shifts even though their source was not edited, because `local` is recomputed globally. The acceptance is: summing `lcc-total` over this metric-derived touched set, the after total is strictly less than the before total, with each unit `u` identified by `(ns, var, arity, line)` (the selector's unique join key, so null-arity `defmethod` units do not collapse together): `{u | before(u) != after(u)}`, then `sum after < sum before`.\n   - Architectural no-regression (A3 — enforcing gate flags). Run `bb gordian gate --baseline munera/open/NNN-slug/before-diagnose.edn --fail-on new-cycles,new-high-findings --max-new-medium-findings 0`. The bare `gate --baseline` only EVALUATES checks; the `--fail-on` flag is what makes new cycles and new high findings FAIL (non-zero exit), and `--max-new-medium-findings 0` enforces the \"no new medium findings\" half of the claim. The gate must PASS (exit 0) with these flags.\n   - The Phase 0 characterization tests and all existing tests for the affected area are GREEN (same expectations as before the refactor).\n   - The change is minimal, local, and decomplecting.\n\n   Autonomy note: this generated task's design is intentionally authored autonomously (objective, narrow: fixed target + preserve behaviour + objective acceptance); the review-task-design loop iterates ambiguity/architecture/inconsistency in place of live user collaboration.\n\n7. Commit the task creation on the current branch.\n   - Commit the new `munera/open/NNN-slug/` task directory (including both baseline files) on the current branch, so delegated lifecycle child sessions inherit the same worktree and can resolve the emitted task path.\n\n8. Emit a structured handoff as your final response.\n   - Output a compact Markdown summary with these headings exactly:\n     - `## Selection Outcome`\n     - `## Munera Task`\n     - `## Handoff Data`\n   - Under `## Selection Outcome`, summarize the chosen target and its evidence (ns/var/arity, file, line range, lcc-total, cc, gap), and the coverage hint.\n   - Under `## Munera Task`, give the task id/slug and the baselines captured.\n   - Under `## Handoff Data`, include this machine-friendly bullet line:\n     - `munera_task_path:` — the `munera/open/NNN-slug` task path.\n   - You may include `worktree_path:` as informational context, but downstream lifecycle execution must rely on inherited session worktree rather than calling `work-on`.\n   - If a field is not available, omit it rather than inventing it.\n   - End the final response with exactly `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE` so the workflow deterministically continues to design review.\n\nExecution constraints:\n- Work only on the single chosen unit from the `incidental-complexity-finder` selection.\n- Prefer root-cause simplification framing over superficial extraction in the generated design.\n- Do NOT call `work-on`.\n- Do NOT create or switch worktrees.\n- Do NOT create a task when no unit qualifies.\n- Do NOT push or open a PR; this workflow ends with a completed, reviewed task on the current local branch (the user decides on PR).\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from :workflow-input}}}],
   :judge
   {:type :invoke,
    :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
    :args {:text {:from {:step "select-and-create" :output :final-llm-reply}},
           :allowed-statuses ["ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK" "REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "review-task-design"},
        "REPEAT" {:goto :done}}}
  {:name "review-task-design",
   :type :delegate,
   :target "review-task-design",
   :prompt-string {:type :map,
                   :fields {:input {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}},
   :context [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}]}
  {:name "create-task-plan",
   :type :delegate,
   :target "create-task-plan",
   :prompt-string {:type :map,
                   :fields {:input {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}},
   :context [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "review-task-design" :yield :text}}]}
  {:name "review-task-plan",
   :type :delegate,
   :target "review-task-plan",
   :prompt-string {:type :map,
                   :fields {:input {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}},
   :context [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "review-task-design" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "create-task-plan" :yield :text}}]}
  {:name "clean-baseline",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :skills ["testing-without-mocks"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "review-task-design" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "create-task-plan" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "review-task-plan" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Establish the pre-characterization clean-source baseline for the incidental-complexity Munera task described by {{input}}. Work only in the invoking session's current inherited worktree. Do NOT call `work-on`, create a worktree, or switch branches.\n\nRequired procedure:\n1. Read the task artifacts (`design.md`, `plan.md`, `steps.md`, `implementation.md`) and identify the target/source path(s) for the selected unit. If the target/source paths cannot be identified from the task artifacts, append a durable failure finding to task artifacts, commit that task-artifact update, and stop with `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n2. Inspect `git status --short` and verify the identified target/source paths are not already dirty before baseline recording. Pre-existing dirty task-artifact or documentation files may remain only when explicitly classified in the task artifacts; pre-existing dirty target/source changes must be appended as a durable failure finding in task artifacts, committed, and must stop the workflow instead of being absorbed into the unmodified-behavior baseline.\n3. Write `characterization-baseline.edn` in the task directory. It must include at least the recorded git `HEAD`, `git status --short`, the target/source paths identified by the task, and any explicitly classified pre-existing task-artifact-or-doc dirt.\n4. Update `implementation.md` tersely with the clean-baseline result and commit any new task-artifact update.\n5. End with exactly one line: `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE` when the baseline was recorded and target/source paths were clean; otherwise `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK` only after the missing-path or dirty-path failure finding has been recorded in task artifacts and committed.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
           :args {:text {:from {:step "clean-baseline" :output :final-llm-reply}},
                  :allowed-statuses ["ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK" "REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "coverage-review"},
        "REPEAT" {:goto "terminal-stop-summary"}}}
  {:name "coverage-review",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :skills ["task-test-review" "testing-without-mocks"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "clean-baseline" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Review the pre-simplification characterization-test net for the incidental-complexity Munera task described by {{input}}. This is a Phase 0 gate before simplification. Do NOT perform simplification or refactor work. Do NOT call `work-on`; use the current inherited worktree.\n\nRequired procedure:\n1. Read the task artifacts and `characterization-baseline.edn`. Confirm the target unit and observable behavior under review are clear.\n2. Inspect existing and newly-added tests for the target's externally observable state or outputs. Cover nominal, edge, and boundary behavior relevant to the target. Follow `testing-without-mocks`: prefer state/output assertions and avoid interaction assertions unless the interaction is itself the observable behavior.\n3. Run the relevant tests needed to prove the characterization net is green against the unmodified target behavior.\n4. If coverage is sufficient and green, record the reviewed coverage and result in task artifacts, commit the task-artifact update, then end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE`.\n5. If fixable characterization gaps remain, record exactly `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS: FIXABLE_GAPS` in the task artifacts with the concrete coverage work required, commit the task-artifact update, then end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n6. If sufficient characterization is infeasible, record exactly `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS: INFEASIBLE` in the task artifacts with the reason, commit the task-artifact update, and do not proceed toward simplification, then end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
           :args {:text {:from {:step "coverage-review" :output :final-llm-reply}},
                  :allowed-statuses ["ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK" "REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "diff-gate"},
        "REPEAT" {:goto "coverage-disposition"}}}
  {:name "coverage-disposition",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "coverage-review" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Determine the next route for the failed characterization-test-net review for {{input}}. Read the task artifacts and the preceding coverage-review output.\n\nIf the task artifacts record exactly `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS: FIXABLE_GAPS`, report that a constrained coverage-fix pass should run and end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE`.\n\nIf the task artifacts record exactly `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS: INFEASIBLE`, or if neither marker is present, report that the workflow must stop before simplification and end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n\nDo not edit source code. Do not perform coverage fixes here. Do not call `work-on`.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
           :args {:text {:from {:step "coverage-disposition" :output :final-llm-reply}},
                  :allowed-statuses ["ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK" "REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "coverage-fix"},
        "REPEAT" {:goto "terminal-stop-summary"}}}
  {:name "coverage-fix",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :skills ["clojure-coding-standards" "testing-without-mocks"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "coverage-review" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "coverage-disposition" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Execute only the next constrained characterization-test-net fix for the incidental-complexity Munera task described by {{input}}. This pass exists before simplification, so it may add characterization tests and explicitly justified minimal testability seams only.\n\nHard constraints:\n- Do NOT simplify, refactor, decomplect, rename, extract, reorganize, or otherwise improve the target implementation.\n- Do NOT perform unrelated cleanup.\n- Do NOT weaken existing expectations.\n- Do NOT make broad production edits. Any production change must be an explicitly justified minimal testability seam recorded in `implementation.md`.\n- Assert externally observable state or outputs; avoid interaction assertions unless the interaction is itself observable behavior.\n- Use the current inherited worktree. Do NOT call `work-on`, create a worktree, or switch branches.\n\nRequired procedure:\n1. Read the task artifacts and the latest coverage-review findings.\n2. Add/refine characterization tests for the recorded nominal, edge, or boundary gaps, or add one explicitly justified minimal testability seam if tests cannot otherwise observe behavior.\n3. Run the relevant tests and keep them green against current behavior.\n4. Update `steps.md`/`implementation.md` with what was added, including any minimal seam justification.\n5. Commit the characterization-fix changes.\n6. End with exactly `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE` so coverage review runs again.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
           :args {:text {:from {:step "coverage-fix" :output :final-llm-reply}},
                  :allowed-statuses ["REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "coverage-review"}}}
  {:name "diff-gate",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash" "edit" "write"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "clean-baseline" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "coverage-review" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Run the workflow-level pre-simplification baseline/diff gate for the incidental-complexity Munera task described by {{input}}. This gate runs after characterization coverage is reviewed complete and before `implement-task`. Work in the current inherited worktree; do NOT call `work-on`, create a worktree, or switch branches.\n\nRequired procedure:\n1. Read the task artifacts and task-local `characterization-baseline.edn`. If the file is missing or lacks recorded HEAD, status, and target/source paths, stop.\n2. Verify the baseline did not include dirty target/source paths at baseline time. If it did, stop before simplification.\n3. Compare both committed changes since the baseline HEAD (`git diff <baseline-head>...HEAD` or an equivalent committed-change comparison) and the current uncommitted worktree status/diff. Coverage-fix commits must not hide coverage-phase edits behind an empty uncommitted `git diff`.\n4. Classify every coverage-phase change. Allowed categories are only: characterization tests, task artifacts, docs, and explicitly justified minimal testability seams.\n5. Stop before simplification if any change is an unclassified source/target change, broad production edit, premature simplification/refactor, missing baseline data, or `CHARACTERIZATION_STATUS: INFEASIBLE`. Record whether the change must be reverted, split, or the task closed, and commit the task-artifact update.\n6. If and only if all coverage-phase changes are allowed and relevant tests are green, record the diff-gate classification in task artifacts, commit the task-artifact update, and end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: REVIEW_COMPLETE`. Otherwise end with exactly `PASS_STATUS: ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK`.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/pass-status-routing",
           :args {:text {:from {:step "diff-gate" :output :final-llm-reply}},
                  :allowed-statuses ["ACTIONABLE_FEEDBACK" "REVIEW_COMPLETE"]}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto "implement-task"},
        "REPEAT" {:goto "terminal-stop-summary"}}}
  {:name "implement-task",
   :type :delegate,
   :target "implement-task",
   :prompt-string {:type :map,
                   :fields {:input {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}},
   :context [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "diff-gate" :yield :text}}]}
  {:name "review-task-implementation",
   :type :delegate,
   :target "review-task-implementation",
   :prompt-string {:type :map,
                   :fields {:input {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}},
   :context [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "clean-baseline" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "coverage-review" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "diff-gate" :yield :text}}
             {:type :source, :from {:step "implement-task" :yield :text}}]}
  {:name "final-summary",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "clean-baseline" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "coverage-review" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "diff-gate" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "implement-task" :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "review-task-implementation" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Produce the user-facing final result for the completed target-present reduce-incidental-complexity run described by {{input}}. Independently inspect the Munera task artifacts. Summarize the design → plan → characterization-test-net gate → baseline/diff gate → simplification implementation → implementation review outcome. Include verification performed, task artifact files updated, commit ids evident from step outputs, and whether the task remains open or was closed. Do not claim a PR was opened or pushed.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge {:type :invoke,
           :operation "workflow/constant-routing",
           :args {:route "DONE"}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto :done}}}
  {:name "terminal-stop-summary",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text "Produce a terminal stop summary for the target-present reduce-incidental-complexity run described by {{input}}. This summary is only for gate failures after a target task exists: dirty baseline, missing target/source baseline data, infeasible characterization, or a failed baseline/diff classification. No-target runs route directly from `select-and-create` to workflow completion and must not run this step.\n\nInspect the task artifacts and prior gate outputs recorded there. Report why simplification did not run, what task artifacts were updated, and whether the next action is revert, split, close, or retry coverage work. Do not claim `implement-task`, simplification, implementation review, push, or PR creation occurred.\n\nInput:\n{{input}}",
     :vars {"input" {:from {:step "select-and-create" :yield :text}}}}]}],
 :name "reduce-incidental-complexity",
 :description
 "Select the single highest incidental-complexity unit, open a constrained behaviour-preserving refactor task in the current worktree, enforce a pre-simplification characterization-test-net gate, and then drive simplification through implementation and review"}
